@page "/"
@page "/movies"

@* Placeholder from Task 2, so that "/" and the nav link have a real page to land on. Task 5 onward fills it.
   Keep the h1 and the PageTitle OUTSIDE any @if (loaded) branch: FocusOnNavigate fires once after the first
   render and never retries, and movies.json arrives long after that. *@
<PageTitle>Films - Film and TV library</PageTitle>

@* tabindex="-1" is not for FocusOnNavigate, which adds it itself: focusBySelector reads
   `if (!element.hasAttribute('tabindex')) { element.tabIndex = -1 }` before focusing. It is for whatever
   replaces FocusOnNavigate later. ElementReference.FocusAsync() does NOT add it, and on an element that
   cannot take focus it fails silently - no exception, no moved focus, no failing test. Declaring it here
   means the heading is reachable by any focus mechanism, not just the one in use today. *@
<h1 tabindex="-1">Films</h1>

<p>The film library is being built.</p>
